# Adding New Features - Complete Guide

Follow this checklist to add a new entity/feature to the codebase. See also: `onion-architecture.mdc`, `usecase-pattern.mdc`, `repository-pattern.mdc`, `controller-pattern.mdc`.

## Prerequisites

- [ ] Entity definition planned (fields, relationships)
- [ ] Database schema updated (Prisma migration created)
- [ ] Business logic requirements clear

## 1. Define Domain Entity

**Location:** `src/entities/{entity-name}/{entity-name}.ts`

```typescript
export interface Entity {
  id: string;
  field: string;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
}
```

**Input interfaces** (in `src/entities/{entity-name}/`):

- `create-{entity}-input.ts`: `export interface CreateEntityInput { field: string; }`
- `update-{entity}-input.ts`: `export interface UpdateEntityInput { id: string; field?: string; }`
- Other inputs as needed: `get-all-...-input.ts`, `get-entity-by-id-input.ts`, `delete-entity-input.ts`

All types live in entities; use case files only import them.

## 2. Repository Layer

- Mapper: `src/repositories/{entity-name}/mappers/{entity-name}.mapper.ts` (Prisma model → Entity)
- Operations: `create.ts`, `get-all.ts`, `get-by-id.ts`, `update.ts`, `delete.ts` in `src/repositories/{entity-name}/`
- Aggregator: `index.ts`; add to `src/repositories/index.ts`

Pattern: `init{Operation}{Entity}Repository(prisma)`; always map to domain entity via `toEntity`.

## 3. Use Case Layer

- Files in `src/usecases/{entity-name}/`: `create-{entity}.ts`, `get-all-{entities}.ts`, `get-{entity}-by-id.ts`, `update-{entity}.ts`, `delete-{entity}.ts`
- **No types in use case files** — import input types from `@/entities/{entity}/...`
- Imports order: Joi, AppContext, entity/input from entities, errors
- First line in body: `validateInput(input);` (with `// Validation` comment)
- Private `validateInput` at bottom; Joi schema defined inside it
- Aggregator: `index.ts`; add to `src/usecases/index.ts`

## 4. REST Layer

- DTOs: `src/rest/{entity-name}/dtos/` — `{entity}.dto.ts`, `create-{entity}.dto.ts`, `update-{entity}.dto.ts` (Zod)
- Mapper: `src/rest/{entity-name}/mappers/{entity}.mapper.ts` — `toDto(entity)`
- Controller: `src/rest/{entity-name}/controllers/{entity}.controller.ts` — all methods in one file, `init{Entity}Controllers(usecases)`
- Routes: `src/rest/{entity-name}/routes.ts`; add to `src/rest/routes.ts`

## 5. OpenAPI (Optional)

Add endpoints to `src/docs/api/openapi.yaml`.

## Naming Conventions

- **Files:** kebab-case (`create-user.ts`)
- **Types:** PascalCase (`CreateUserInput`)
- **Functions:** camelCase (`createUser`)
- **Factories:** `init{Entity}{Type}` (`initUserRepositories`, `initUserUsecases`, `initUserControllers`)

## Complete Checklist

- [ ] **Domain:** Entity + input interfaces in `src/entities/{entity}/`
- [ ] **Repository:** Mapper, operations, aggregator, register in `repositories/index.ts`
- [ ] **Use case:** Operations (no types in files), aggregator, register in `usecases/index.ts`
- [ ] **REST:** DTOs, mapper, controller, routes, register in `rest/routes.ts`
- [ ] **Docs:** OpenAPI (optional)
